    given-names: "Manuel Enrique"
    affiliation: "Guanes Health Collective"
title: "Guanes Health Simulation Suite: Biophysical and Systemic In Silico Modeling for Cancer Immunotherapy"
version: 6.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-25
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22101265"
url: "https://health.guanes.biz"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Manuelenriquep/Guanes-Health"
license-url: "https://github.com/Manuelenriquep/Guanes-Health/blob/main/LICENSE"
type: software
abstract: >-
  Guanes Health is a deterministic computational systems biology framework and research
  instrument (Layer B / Layer A calibration) modeling the multi-scale coupling between
  gut mucosal barrier integrity (Akkermansia muciniphila), portal endotoxemia (IL-6 / STAT3 /
  PD-L1 / TOX epigenetic silencing), and local tumor microenvironment biophysics
  (extracellular acidosis, NHE1/MCT1/MCT4 proton transport kinetics, and CAR-T cellular bioenergetics).
keywords:
  - "computational oncology"
  - "systems biology"
  - "biophysical modeling"
  - "tumor microenvironment"
  - "acidosis"
  - "car-t therapy"
  - "nhe1"
  - "akkermansia muciniphila"
  - "epigenetic exhaustion"
  - "fail-closed logic"
